Well... Ideally you two should figure it out directly before I put any
continuous effort into either project.
On Jan 29, 2013 2:24 AM, "la gleki" <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com> wrote:

>
>
> On Sunday, January 27, 2013 11:43:48 PM UTC+4, Feilen Haksan wrote:
>>
>> So... for the time being, I've got an enormous amount of free time on my
>> hands, and am very interested in modernizing the lojban website. If anyone
>> has a specific workload in mind that they'd like to see on the wiki, let me
>> know and I'll see what I can do about it :D
>
>
>
> So. Idlework from the irc chat is working on a CMS based on Django. It's
> going to be not just a wiki but rather an intergration of jvs, wiki,
> CLL.....
> Good luck to him.
>
> However, don't you think that there is a problem here, namely a split of
> efforts?
>
> We can't be sure whether he finishes this project and we shouldn't wait
> either.
>
> So I suggest once again leaving the old wiki as it is.
>
>
> Now let's think that Lojban has been just born. What do we need for a wiki?
>
> 1. Textbook (the Waves) and a link to CLL.
> 2. Texts, multimedia with links to them.
> 3. Some brief informaton about the history of the language.
> 4. Some brief information about the difference between CLL and the current
> state of affairs (but it's better to move it into the Waves).
>
>
> That's all! Have I missed something?
>
> This is how we can start working on the new wiki (mw.lojban.org).
>
> If Idelwork succeeds then we'll transfer the content of LMW and the whoe
> jvs database into his project.
> Until then let's use the best we have.
>
> Feilen, I hope these 4 items are clear enough. Make the wiki the way you
> would like it to be.
> And don't be shy. Ask questions here :)
